====Verb====
{{en-verb|hogg}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[greedily]] take more than one's share, to take precedence at the expense of another or others.
#* '''2000''' DiCamillo, Kate ''Because of Winn-Dixie'', Scholastic Inc., New York, Ch 15:
#*: The [...] air-conditioning unit didn't work very good, and there was only one fan; and from the minute me and Winn-Dixie got in the library, he '''hogged''' it all.
#: ''Hey! Quit '''hogging''' all the blankets.''
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[clip]] the [[mane]] of a [[horse]], making it short and bristly.
#: {{rfquotek|Smart}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} To [[scrub]] with a hog, or scrubbing broom.
# {{lb|en|transitive|nautical}} To cause the [[keel]] of a ship to [[arch]] upwards (the opposite of {{m|en|sag}}).

